WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:09.837
NIST SP 800-63-4, final since July
31, 2025, separates three scales.

2
00:00:09.837 --> 00:00:14.338
Identity proofing is usually done by
the partner, under its own practice.

3
00:00:14.338 --> 00:00:17.900
Authentication is done by the
partner's identity service.

4
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:23.650
Federation assurance is set by the agency,
as relying party, for each application.

5
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:30.288
SP 800-63C-4 says what each
federation level demands.

6
00:00:30.288 --> 00:00:33.671
At level one, the identity
provider signs the assertion,

7
00:00:33.671 --> 00:00:37.349
and the relying party validates
it against the expected key,

8
00:00:37.349 --> 00:00:41.688
with the assertion audience-restricted
and protected against replay.

9
00:00:41.688 --> 00:00:46.525
Level two adds injection protection, a
transaction the relying party starts,

10
00:00:46.525 --> 00:00:51.664
an assertion for a single relying party,
a trust agreement established in advance,

11
00:00:51.664 --> 00:00:54.838
and identifiers without
plaintext personal data.

12
00:00:54.838 --> 00:00:58.537
Level three adds holder-of-key
or a bound authenticator.

13
00:00:58.537 --> 00:01:03.645
Selection follows NIST's steps: assess
impact per user group, take the initial

14
00:01:03.645 --> 00:01:09.151
levels, tailor, and document the result in
a Digital Identity Acceptance Statement.

15
00:01:09.151 --> 00:01:11.725
The chapter didn't read the October 6,

16
00:01:11.725 --> 00:01:19.610
2026 planning note on SP 800-63C-4
in full, so check it first.
